#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0337 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), MCRIT1(Char). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | RESPONSE`. The mirror of scenario 1: the COMPANION MCRIT1 is declared and the CONDITION variable MCRIT1ML is not, so the first conjunct `var_exists('MCRIT1ML')` is FALSE and the rule stays silent. This is the DISCRIMINATING direction test - it is the scenario that fails if the two operands are ever swapped. The rule still EXECUTES (expect=noViolation, not skipped) because `MCRITy` matches MCRIT1 and seeds the tuple y=1; MCRIT1ML is then synthesised as absent."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col MCRIT1 type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | RESPONSE
